flowchart TB
  accTitle: Where the chooser of new issues leads
  accDescr: On New issue, GitHub shows the chooser that install writes for a repository without forms, with blank issues turned off. A bug report and a feature request each open a form, whose answers choose the labels before the first analysis. A question goes to the discussions, a vulnerability to a private report, and the link of the support says what happens with an issue
  new(["`**New issue**<br>on GitHub`"]) --> chooser["the chooser, config.yml,<br>with blank issues turned off"]
  chooser --> forms
  chooser --> links
  subgraph forms ["an issue, from a form"]
    direction TB
    bug["Bug report,<br>bug_report.yml"]
    feature["Feature request,<br>feature_request.yml"]
    bug ~~~ feature
  end
  subgraph links ["no issue, from a link"]
    direction TB
    question["Question: the first category<br>of answer_categories<br>in the discussions"]
    vulnerability["Security vulnerability:<br>a private report"]
    support["Support: SUPPORT.md"]
    question ~~~ vulnerability ~~~ support
  end
  forms --> analysis(["`labels from the form,<br>then the **first analysis**`"])
  classDef trigger fill:#d4a72c33,stroke:#bf8700,stroke-width:2px
  classDef job fill:#8c959f1f,stroke:#8c959f,stroke-width:2px
  classDef person fill:#0969da26,stroke:#0969da,stroke-width:2px
  classDef safe fill:#1a7f3726,stroke:#1a7f37,stroke-width:2px
  class new trigger
  class chooser job
  class bug,feature,question,vulnerability,support person
  class analysis safe
